{
  "name": "bumblebee",
  "_about": "A bumblebee -- the buff-tailed bumblebee (Bombus terrestris), a worker 17 mm long: round and dense with fur, black with a dark-yellow collar across the front of the thorax and a second yellow band across the gaster, the tail buff-white; a short head, hairy all over; short elbowed antennae; black hairy legs, the hind ones with pollen baskets (the variant \"with pollen\"); small smoky-brown wings, folded back over the gaster at rest. Coats: the white-tailed and the red-tailed bumblebee. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/winged/hymen.py on insectlib.py + wlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait, elbowed antennae that wave, the wings folded flat over the abdomen -- swung out and beating in the variant \"flying\").",
